{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>If there is over him an angel</b> — to declare to a man. <b>For a man</b> [בעד אדם], like: <i>they say to me, he is my brother</i> [אמרי לי אחי הוא]. From this verse is a teaching: that the angels who bring death, who seek a person's life, are many, and one angel is appointed over him to guard him. And the one who understands the sod of the array of the hosts will acknowledge this."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:22.573518596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}